I am setting up Multiple Instance Infrastructure using Terraform Iac for Multi-VM Project

Provider
aws : us-east-1

CPU Type, OS, Security Groups and their Inbound Rules for 5 Instance, I am creating are :

Nginx	
    t2.micro
    Ubuntu 22.04 LTS
    Allow HTTP (80), HTTPS (443), SSH (22) from anywhere.
    Acts as a reverse proxy; low CPU/memory usage.

Apache Tomcat	
    t2.small
    Ubuntu 22.04 LTS
    Allow 8080 (for web apps) from Nginx only, SSH (22) from trusted IPs.
    Requires more resources for Java applications.

MySQL	
    t3.small
    Amazon Linux 2
    Allow 3306 from Tomcat/RabbitMQ only, SSH (22) from trusted IPs.
    Needs higher RAM & storage for database performance.

RabbitMQ	
    t2.micro
    Ubuntu 22.04 LTS
    Allow 5672 (AMQP) and 15672 (management UI) from Tomcat, SSH (22) from trusted IPs.
    Lightweight message broker; low CPU/memory needs.

Memcached
    t2.micro
    Ubuntu 22.04 LTS
    Allow 11211 (Memcached) from Tomcat/RabbitMQ only, SSH (22) from trusted IPs.
    Caching service; low memory footprint.


